  "description": "Cladding remediation to remove existing combustible facade materials to replace with non-combustible materials.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;External Wall Type performance. The applicant is required to ensure that, in fully or partially replacing the facade system, the following targets are met: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;a) External Thermal Insulation Composite System wall type u value of 0.15&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;b) Cladding panel wall type u value of 0.19&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;c) Aluminium cassette rainscreen wall type u value of 0.22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;d) Aluminium fascia wall type u value of 0.24&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;e) Facing brick wall type u value of 0.28. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For completeness, a Summary Statement highlighting changes supported by detailed justification and assessing their impact between the approved and the as-built figures where applicable should be submitted and approved by the local planning authority at the relevant phase of the development. The development hereby approved shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with the details thereby approved.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: In the interest of addressing climate change and supporting net zero development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
